@*
    Shared grid toolbar: page size + search box.

    site.js reuses this markup when it finds it (attachTable) and builds an
    identical toolbar when a view does not declare one, so the default page size
    lives here and in PAGE_SIZE_DEFAULT in site.js - keep the two in step.

    The Export to Excel button is added by site.js at runtime; it is not declared
    here, so every grid gets it whether or not the view supplies a toolbar.
*@
<div class="table-toolbar">
    <label class="table-page-size-label">
        Show
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm table-page-size">
            <option value="10">10</option>
            <option value="25">25</option>
            <option value="50">50</option>
            <option value="100" selected>100</option>
        </select>
        entries
    </label>
    <input type="search" class="form-control table-search-input" placeholder="Search all columns..." aria-label="Search all columns" autocomplete="off" />
</div>
